This product includes a modified fork of image-webp from the image-rs project,
licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0. The fork branches from image-rs/image-webp at
commit f4d80bd (after the 0.2.4 release) and adds seventeen commits: a VP8 lossy
still-image encoder — per-macroblock intra prediction chosen by rate-distortion
cost, coefficient-free macroblock skipping, a nonlinear quality-to-quantizer
curve, and quantizer-proportional loop filtering — alongside lossless encoder,
decoder, and animation fixes. On top of those, the fork keeps nanoraster's
deterministic Huffman tie-break, which holds lossless output identical between
32-bit and 64-bit targets. Its source and license text are retained under
rust/vendor/image-webp/.

This product includes wgpu-hal 30.0.0 from the gfx-rs/wgpu project, licensed
under MIT OR Apache-2.0, with one nanoraster patch: Direct3D 12 pipeline state
stream subobjects are aligned to the pointer size rather than to eight bytes,
which lets the DX12 backend create pipelines on 32-bit Windows. Its source and
license text are retained under rust/vendor/wgpu-hal/.

This product adapts the thin-film Fresnel model from the Khronos glTF Sample
Renderer, developed by UX3D and contributors, licensed under Apache-2.0.
Source: https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glTF-Sample-Renderer/blob/cc27919cacbb235d2f58a0c0203387efce9375f8/source/Renderer/shaders/iridescence.glsl
The adaptation in rust/render-core/src/physical.wgsl changes GLSL to WGSL and
uses the nanoraster material/uniform contract. The Apache-2.0 license text
is included in this distribution's license file.

The 128×128 blue-noise RGBA texture in rust/render-core/assets/ is decoded
from n8ao 1.10.2 src/BlueNoise.js, released under CC0 1.0 Universal.
Source: https://unpkg.com/n8ao@1.10.2/src/BlueNoise.js
Decoded SHA-256: b9efcfbc51ecafe80db33a5b0c9577f978a18bb7c0eb72777fe8a0a4205fd1ac

The GGX/DFG, sheen, CubeUV, transmission filtering and PBR Neutral routines in
physical.wgsl, lighting.wgsl and shader.wgsl are adapted from Three.js r184.
The embedded neutral-room PMREM derives from its RoomEnvironment and the DFG
lookup table from its DFGLUTData. GLSL was ported to WGSL; room radiance was
repacked to one channel and quantized. Exact source fingerprints, generation
instructions and asset hashes are retained in rust/render-core/assets/.
Source: https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/tree/r184

